{
  "comment": "Scenarios of tests/abi/resize_observation.py and its Chromium oracle resize_observation_browser.mjs. Each step runs in order; update is one rendering update (Chromium: an animation frame and a task; native: rv_host_update) and logs '|'; settle is two updates without a mark, for intersection observer tasks that Chromium queues after the frame. A delivery logs '<observer>:<target ids>' and its entries; arm runs a step once when the observer next delivers an entry for the target. Observers are created in their first-observe order, except in observerOrder.",
  "markup": "<!doctype html><html><head><style>body{margin:0}.b{box-sizing:content-box;width:100px;height:50px;padding:10px 4px 6px 2px;border:5px solid black;margin:3px}.v{writing-mode:vertical-rl}.z{zoom:2}.f{width:100.5px;height:33.25px}.bb{box-sizing:border-box;width:100px;height:50px;padding:10px;border:5px solid black}</style></head><body><div id=a class=b></div><div id=v class=\"b v\"></div><div id=z class=\"b z\"></div><div id=f class=\"b f\"></div><div id=bb class=bb></div><span id=inl>inline</span><div id=hid style=\"display:none\"></div><svg id=svg width=200 height=100><rect id=r x=10 y=20 width=30 height=40 /></svg><div id=outer style=\"width:200px\"><div id=mid style=\"width:150px\"><div id=deep style=\"width:100px;height:10px\"></div></div></div></body></html>",
